Z||000000||LateBloomFiero||08-14-2001||10:22 PM||||Bought an 86 SE with the aero nose.  Sometime in its previous life the left front corner had an impact with the immovable object and the bottom of the nose was pushed in.  I liberated the nose tonight and pushed it back out.  Unfortunately it had been pushed in far too long because it seems to have taken a "set".  Will it eventually relax to original shape, would applying heat help to restore the original shape?<P>Additional question:  is the metal support behind the energy absorber assy. the same between a aero nose and a coupe?  <P>TIA<BR>Bill||||reg||5
Z||000001||mbramble||08-14-2001||10:27 PM||||I don't know about reshaping the nose but the metal bracket is the same for all cars.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||08-14-2001||10:33 PM||||I was told to use heat to put it back in shape, i would never do this but thats what i was told by a few body shops... kinda makes sence a little bit... if your paint aint mint might want to try it<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000003||grinthock||08-14-2001||10:36 PM||||actually I got a minor DING in my front fascia on my 85, The fieroshop told me to and I quote "Give it a bath" they told me to put it in WARM water, and slowly warm it up...  So I did, it popped right back out.. Then they told me to cool it down slowly.<P>They did say, DO NOT DO NOT DO NOT use a heat gun.||||reg||1
